{"name":"Desert Palm","hex":"#675239","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"desert","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A barren area of land or desolate terrain, especially one with little water or vegetation; a wasteland.\n\nIn particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground.","In particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Usually of a place: abandoned, deserted, or uninhabited."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desert"},{"term":"palm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various evergreen trees from the family Palmae or Arecaceae, which are mainly found in the tropics.","A branch or leaf of the palm, anciently borne or worn as a symbol of victory or rejoicing."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The inner and somewhat concave part of the human hand or other primate hand that extends from the wrist to the bases of the fingers.","The corresponding part of the forefoot of a nonprimate mammal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Desert","blocks":[{"text":"A desert is a landscape where little precipitation occurs and, consequently, living conditions create unique biomes and ecosystems. The lack of vegetation exposes the unprotected surface of the ground to denudation. About one-third of the land surface of the Earth is arid or semi-arid. This includes much of the polar regions, where little precipitation occurs, and which are sometimes called polar deserts or \"cold deserts\". Deserts can be classified by the amount of precipitation that falls, by the temperature that prevails, by the causes of desertification or by their geographical location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG/330px-Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/500px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/1280px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/500px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A camel shepherd in southern Tunisia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGroupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Deserts.png/500px-Deserts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Deserts.png/1280px-Deserts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Deserts.png/500px-Deserts.pn